   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T88"><text:span text:style-name="T52">NOTE</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">: changer la taille de police dans le tiroir de navigation, aller à </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Apparence </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T72">&lt;unk&gt;</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52"> Interface </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T72">&lt;unk&gt;</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52"> Langues</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> et double-cliquez sur une langue de l&apos;interface. Changer le pourcentage de la taille de la police de caractères supérieure ou inférieure</text:span></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P73" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark text:name="_The_Borders_tab"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871150"/>The <text:span text:style-name="T88">Borders</text:span> tab<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871150"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P10" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">You can add a decorative border frame around the text in the app, for example:</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P226" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P3" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr4" draw:name="Picture 193" text:anchor-type="as-char" svg:width="2.2917in" svg:height="4.0102in" draw:z-index="0"><draw:image xlink:href="SAB02/21.png" xlink:type="simple" xlink:show="embed" xlink:actuate="onLoad" draw:mime-type="image/png"/>
     <svg:desc>Screenshot_20160823-104717</svg:desc>
    </draw:frame><text:span text:style-name="T39"><text:s/></text:span><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr4" draw:name="Picture 192" text:anchor-type="as-char" svg:width="2.1772in" svg:height="3.9689in" draw:z-index="0"><draw:image xlink:href="SAB02/22.png" xlink:type="simple" xlink:show="embed" xlink:actuate="onLoad" draw:mime-type="image/png"/>
     <svg:desc>Screenshot_20160823-103941</svg:desc>
    </draw:frame></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P8" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P10" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Vous pouvez sélectionner une bordure dans la galerie d&apos;images de bordure fournies avec le constructeur d&apos;applications bibliques, ou vous pouvez créer votre propre bordure.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P228" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P10" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">To select a border from the border gallery:</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
   <text:list text:style-name="WWNum21">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P375" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Cliquez sur </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">choisissez dans la galerie…</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P375" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Sélectionnez une image dans la galerie et cliquez sur OK.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P241" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr9" draw:name="Picture 191" text:anchor-type="char" svg:x="1.7752in" svg:y="0.0898in" svg:width="2.6252in" svg:height="1.7189in" draw:z-index="329"><draw:image xlink:href="SAB02/23.png" xlink:type="simple" xlink:show="embed" xlink:actuate="onLoad" draw:mime-type="image/png"/>
    </draw:frame><text:s/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P228" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P228" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P228" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:soft-page-break/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P228" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P228" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P228" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P228" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P228" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P10" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Pour ajouter votre propre bordure :</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
   <text:list text:style-name="WWNum45">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P376" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Créer la bordure en tant que fichier image (JPEG ou PNG) en orientation portrait. Assurez-vous que la zone rectangulaire du milieu de l&apos;image est vide. Cette zone vide est où le texte sera affiché.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P190" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr4" draw:name="Picture 190" text:anchor-type="as-char" svg:width="1.722in" svg:height="2.2953in" draw:z-index="0"><draw:image xlink:href="SAB02/24.png" xlink:type="simple" xlink:show="embed" xlink:actuate="onLoad" draw:mime-type="image/png"/>
     <svg:desc>page-border-lines-blank-zSOsPL-clipart</svg:desc>
    </draw:frame><text:span text:style-name="T39"><text:s/></text:span><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr4" draw:name="Picture 189" text:anchor-type="as-char" svg:width="1.5465in" svg:height="2.2953in" draw:z-index="0"><draw:image xlink:href="SAB02/25.png" xlink:type="simple" xlink:show="embed" xlink:actuate="onLoad" draw:mime-type="image/png"/>
     <svg:desc>Border-Decorative-2</svg:desc>
    </draw:frame><text:span text:style-name="T39"><text:s/></text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P348" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39"><text:line-break/>Vous n&apos;avez pas besoin de fournir une image de bordure en orientation paysage. Cela sera généré automatiquement. Peu importe le rapport largeur-hauteur de l&apos;image, car l&apos;application va couper la bordure et l&apos;arranger pour différentes tailles d&apos;écran.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P348" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Essayez de ne pas rendre la bordure trop large, sinon il y aura un espace limité pour afficher le texte.<text:line-break/></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
   <text:list text:continue-numbering="true" text:style-name="WWNum45">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P377" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Go to the </text:span><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_The_Borders_tab" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T55">Appearance</text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T76"></text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T39"> </text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T52">Graphics</text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T39"> </text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T76"></text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T16"> </text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T23">Border</text:span></text:span></text:a><text:span text:style-name="T16"> tab.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P377" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T16">Cliquez sur </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Ajouter une image…</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> et sélectionnez l&apos;image de bord.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P377" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T16">Assurez-vous que la case à cocher </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Inclure une bordure autour du texte dans cette application</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> est sélectionnée.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P377" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T16">If you want to display the border for some books and not others, or on main chapters but not book introductions, go to the Features page for each book and modify the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Show border around text</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> and </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Show border around introduction</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> settings.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P9" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P35" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Scripture App Builder prend le fichier image de bordure que vous fournissez et trouve la zone de rectangle vide à l&apos;intérieur. Il coupe ensuite l&apos;image restante en 8 pièces : coin supérieur gauche , en haut, en haut à droite, à gauche, à droite, en bas à gauche, en bas à gauche, en bas à droite et en bas à droite.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P36" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Lorsque la bordure est affichée sur l&apos;écran de l&apos;application, les images de coin sont mises à l&apos;échelle en fonction de la taille de l&apos;écran, et le côté, les images en haut et en bas sont redimensionnées et étirées pour remplir l&apos;espace entre les coins. De cette façon, la bordure s&apos;adapte à l&apos;affichage avec des tailles d&apos;écran différentes. Cette technique permet à l&apos;application d&apos;afficher la bordure en plein écran ou lorsqu&apos;il y a une barre d&apos;outils en bas de page.</text:span><text:bookmark text:name="_Fonts"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Ref459716708"/><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P73" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871151"/>L&apos;onglet Paramètres des bordures<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871151"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T186"><text:soft-page-break/>Si vous incluez une bordure dans votre application, vous pouvez spécifier si la bordure apparaît séparément autour de chaque panneau, ou autour de la fenêtre entière, y compris la vue à deux volets.<text:span text:style-name="T186"/></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P53" text:outline-level="2"><text:bookmark text:name="_Interface"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871152"/>Interface<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871152"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Le menu Interface vous permet de spécifier dans quelles langues l&apos;interface utilisateur est disponible et comment cette traduction est affichée. Il a trois onglets : Langues, Translations and Layout Direction.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P73" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark text:name="_The_Languages_tab"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871153"/>The <text:span text:style-name="T88">Languages</text:span> tab<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871153"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">L&apos;onglet Langues vous permet de spécifier les langues de l&apos;interface disponibles pour l&apos;utilisateur à sélectionner. Ceci est mieux déterminé en connaissant le public visé par l&apos;application et en choisissant les langues qui répondront à leurs besoins. REMARQUE : cela ne se réfère pas à la langue dans laquelle votre texte biblique ou d&apos;autres ressources du livre sont écrites. </text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">SAB a une liste de langues qui ont déjà des traductions d&apos;interface, couvrant de nombreuses langues nationales du monde, par exemple le français, l&apos;anglais, l&apos;espagnol et le chinois. Vous pouvez choisir les langues à partir desquelles l&apos;utilisateur peut choisir quand il accède aux paramètres de l&apos;application. Utilisez <text:span text:style-name="T51">Ajouter une langue…</text:span> (voir ci-dessous) pour ajouter une langue d&apos;interface et fournir la traduction de tous les termes.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">SAB détectera la langue à laquelle le téléphone de l&apos;utilisateur est configuré. Il s’agit normalement d’une des langues nationales de la liste des SAB. À ce stade, vous pouvez spécifier ce que vous voulez que l&apos;application fasse en utilisant l&apos;un des deux choix :</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T51"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Utiliser la langue du système actuel de l&apos;appareil. Si aucune traduction n&apos;existe dans cette langue, utilisez…</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Sélectionnez cette option pour détecter la langue système actuelle du téléphone et essayez de l&apos;associer à l&apos;une des langues que vous avez fournies. Si le téléphone a une langue qui n&apos;est pas dans votre liste, vous pouvez spécifier la langue par défaut à choisir.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr2" draw:name="Frame9" text:anchor-type="paragraph" svg:x="-0.0035in" svg:y="0.0555in" svg:width="5.9374in" draw:z-index="330" loext:may-break-between-pages="true">
     <draw:text-box fo:min-height="0.0161in">
      <table:table table:name="Table42" table:style-name="Table42">
       <table:table-column table:style-name="Table42.A"/>
       <table:table-column table:style-name="Table42.B"/>
       <table:table-row table:style-name="Table42.1">
        <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table42.A1" office:value-type="string">
         <text:p text:style-name="P269" loext:marker-style-name="T3"><text:span text:style-name="T68">&lt;unk&gt;</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T3"> </text:span></text:p>
        </table:table-cell>
        <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table42.B1" office:value-type="string">
         <text:p text:style-name="P11" loext:marker-style-name="T88"><text:span text:style-name="T88">Recherche où vivent les principales communautés de votre langue locale cible et quelles sont les langues nationales dans ces régions. Fournissez ces langues à votre choix et sélectionnez une langue par défaut. Par exemple, les Loups du Sénégal francophone ont des communautés de diaspora en France et aux États-Unis. Dans ce cas, sélectionnez le français et l’anglais comme langues d’interface disponibles et peut-être sélectionnez le français comme langue par défaut si le téléphone d’un utilisateur n’est pas en français ou en anglais.</text:span></text:p>
        </table:table-cell>
       </table:table-row>
      </table:table>
     </draw:text-box>
    </draw:frame><text:s/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T51"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Utiliser cette langue :</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Utilisez cette option pour forcer l&apos;interface de l&apos;application à apparaître dans une certaine langue, peu importe la configuration du téléphone. Les utilisateurs peuvent toujours changer la langue à l&apos;une des langues que vous avez fournies dans les paramètres de l&apos;application.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr2" draw:name="Frame10" text:anchor-type="paragraph" svg:x="-0.0035in" svg:y="0.0555in" svg:width="5.9374in" draw:z-index="295" loext:may-break-between-pages="true">
     <draw:text-box fo:min-height="0.0161in">
      <table:table table:name="Table43" table:style-name="Table43">
       <table:table-column table:style-name="Table43.A"/>
       <table:table-column table:style-name="Table43.B"/>
       <table:table-row table:style-name="Table43.1">
        <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table43.A1" office:value-type="string">
         <text:p text:style-name="P269" loext:marker-style-name="T3"><text:span text:style-name="T68">&lt;unk&gt;</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T3"> </text:span></text:p>
        </table:table-cell>
        <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table43.B1" office:value-type="string">
         <text:p text:style-name="P11" loext:marker-style-name="T88"><text:span text:style-name="T88">Cette option est utile si votre application contient du texte d&apos;interface ou des ressources de livres (comme des aides bibliques) dans une langue nationale particulière. Ce serait normalement si le public spécifique se trouvait presque exclusivement dans un seul pays avec une seule langue nationale.</text:span></text:p>
        </table:table-cell>
       </table:table-row>
      </table:table>
     </draw:text-box>
    </draw:frame><text:s/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T51"><text:soft-page-break/><text:span text:style-name="T51">Quelles langues de l&apos;interface voulez-vous que les utilisateurs puissent choisir dans les paramètres de l&apos;application ?</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Voici la liste des langues d&apos;interface disponibles. Choisissez tous ceux que vous pensez aider les utilisateurs de l&apos;application, couvrant les pays où il y a des communautés importantes. Inclure un choix de langues n&apos;augmente pas significativement la taille de l&apos;application.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Double-click a language name to specify the <text:span text:style-name="T51">Font</text:span>, <text:span text:style-name="T51">Size</text:span> and <text:span text:style-name="T51">Text Direction</text:span> (i.e. De gauche à droite) que l&apos;interface s&apos;affichera pour cette langue.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T51"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Ajouter la langue…</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Utilisez ce bouton pour ajouter votre propre langue d&apos;interface. Vous spécifiez le nom, le code de langue, la police et la taille par défaut et la direction du texte (pour les langues de droite à gauche). Une fois que vous aurez choisi OK, la nouvelle langue apparaîtra déjà sélectionnée en bas de la liste des langues de l&apos;interface. Cliquez sur l&apos;onglet <text:span text:style-name="T51">Traductions</text:span> pour entrer les noms des éléments d&apos;interface traduits pour cette langue.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P72" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871154"/>The <text:span text:style-name="T88">Translations</text:span> tab<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871154"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">L&apos;onglet <text:span text:style-name="T51">Traductions</text:span> vous permet de modifier les noms des éléments de l&apos;interface dans n&apos;importe quelle langue que vous avez sélectionnée pour être disponible dans l&apos;application. Si vous avez ajouté votre propre langue, elle apparaîtra dans l&apos;onglet le plus à droite.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Utilisez le bouton <text:span text:style-name="T51">Exporter</text:span> pour exporter un fichier texte avec tous les éléments de l&apos;interface à traduire, dans chacune des langues disponibles. Ceci est utile si vous voulez donner la liste à quelqu&apos;un d&apos;autre à traduire. Si vous avez ajouté votre propre langue, vous devrez peut-être entrer son code et sa traduction pour chaque élément. Par ex. si j&apos;ajoute le langage Wolof et le code « loup » (en utilisant le bouton <text:span text:style-name="T51">Ajouter la langue</text:span> dans l&apos;onglet <text:span text:style-name="T51">Langues</text:span> , puis exporter la liste des traductions de l&apos;interface en utilisant le bouton <text:span text:style-name="T51">Exporter</text:span> , je peux ajouter les traductions Wolof . Dans le fichier texte exporté, chaque élément de l&apos;interface a un en-tête (par ex.<text:span text:style-name="T51"> $ Menu_Bible</text:span>) suivi d&apos;une liste de codes de langue et de leur traduction pour l&apos;élément d&apos;interface <text:span text:style-name="T51">Menu_Bible</text:span>. À la fin de la liste pour <text:span text:style-name="T51">Menu_Bible</text:span> je peux ajouter une ligne <text:span text:style-name="T51">loup : Injil</text:span>. Je peux ensuite le faire pour tous les éléments de l&apos;interface.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Une fois la liste terminée, utilisez le bouton <text:span text:style-name="T51">Importer</text:span> pour importer les modifications dans SAB.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P72" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark text:name="_The_Layout_Direction"/><text:bookmark text:name="_Layout_Direction"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871155"/>L&apos;onglet <text:span text:style-name="T88">Direction</text:span> de mise en page<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871155"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">La direction de la mise en page de l&apos;interface utilisateur affecte la position du nom du livre dans le menu et le côté duquel le panneau de navigation glisse. Il y a quatre options:</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:list text:style-name="WWNum90">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P117"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Gauche à Droite</text:span> – par défaut, avec le nom du livre affiché en haut à gauche et le tiroir de navigation glissant du côté gauche.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P117"><text:soft-page-break/><text:span text:style-name="T51">Droite à Gauche</text:span> – avec le nom du livre affiché en haut à droite et le tiroir de navigation glissant du côté droit.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P117"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Utiliser la direction à partir de la langue actuelle de l&apos;interface utilisateur</text:span>. Si la langue actuelle est normalement écrite dans une certaine direction, l&apos;application reflétera ce paramètre. Cela signifie qu&apos;un utilisateur peut changer la langue de l&apos;application dans les paramètres et que l&apos;application répondra avec la direction de l&apos;interface utilisateur.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P117"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Utiliser la direction du texte affiché</text:span>. Cela dépendra du texte du livre affiché dans la zone de l’écran, ou de l’écran supérieur dans la vue à deux volets. Voir <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_Setting_a_specific" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Définir la direction de texte d&apos;un livre spécifique</text:span></text:span></text:a><text:span text:style-name="T51">.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P52" text:outline-level="2"><text:bookmark text:name="_Colors"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871156"/>Couleurs<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871156"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Le menu Couleurs vous permet de personnaliser presque toutes les couleurs de votre application. L&apos;onglet <text:span text:style-name="T51">Couleurs</text:span> vous permet de définir un aspect global et de personnaliser davantage les couleurs à l&apos;aide des onglets <text:span text:style-name="T51">Couleurs</text:span> et <text:span text:style-name="T51">Couleurs de livre</text:span>.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P72" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark text:name="_The_Color_Scheme"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871157"/>The <text:span text:style-name="T88">Color Scheme</text:span> tab<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871157"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">SAB est livré avec environ 28 couleurs préfabriquées. Le schéma de couleurs affecte la barre de menu, les icônes de la barre de navigation du bas, les curseurs de police, les onglets de sélection du livre et la couleur du texte du titre. Cliquez sur le schéma que vous voulez et choisissez ensuite les thèmes (Normal, Sepia, Dark, Rose, Sage et Charcoal) auxquels l&apos;utilisateur aura accès. These will appear under the text size (<text:span text:style-name="T45">A</text:span>A) icon on the menu bar.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"><text:s/></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P72" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871158"/>The <text:span text:style-name="T88">Main Colors</text:span> tab<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871158"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">L&apos;onglet Couleurs Principales vous permet de personnaliser tous les paramètres de couleurs nommés pour tous les six thèmes (Normal, Sepia, Dark, Rose, Sage et Charbon). Double-cliquez sur une entrée de couleur pour afficher la boîte de dialogue de sélection <text:span text:style-name="T51">Modifier la couleur</text:span> pour les trois thèmes. Utilisez <text:span text:style-name="T51">Sélectionnez la couleur…</text:span> pour lancer le sélecteur de couleurs pour chaque entrée de thème.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P72" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark text:name="_The_Book_Colors"/><text:bookmark text:name="_Book_Colors"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871159"/>The <text:span text:style-name="T88">Book Colors</text:span> Onglet<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871159"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">L&apos;onglet Livres Couleurs vous permet de spécifier les couleurs d&apos;arrière-plan de la tuile dans la vue Grille du sélecteur de livre (sur le menu principal de l&apos;application). Si votre application n&apos;a pas de livres d&apos;Écriture, cet onglet sera vide.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">The Grid View regroupe les livres bibliques par catégorie, par exemple Pentateuch, Historique, Évangile, PaulineEpistle. Vous pouvez spécifier la couleur de fond pour chaque catégorie et pour les six thèmes. Double-cliquez sur une catégorie pour afficher la boîte de dialogue de sélection <text:span text:style-name="T51">Modifier la couleur</text:span> pour les six thèmes. Utilisez <text:span text:style-name="T51">Sélectionnez la couleur…</text:span> pour lancer le sélecteur de couleurs pour chaque entrée de thème.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P52" text:outline-level="2"><text:bookmark text:name="_Fonts_1"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871160"/>Polices<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871160"/><text:bookmark-end text:name="_Ref459716708"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"><text:soft-page-break/>Avec les différents onglets du menu du projet <text:span text:style-name="T51">Fontes</text:span> SAB vous permet de spécifier une ou plusieurs polices à utiliser dans l&apos;application et de spécifier un ou plusieurs claviers et modèles lexicaux pour aider les utilisateurs à écrire dans leur langue.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P72" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark text:name="_The_Main_Font"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871161"/>The <text:span text:style-name="T88">Main Font</text:span> tab<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871161"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">SAB allows you to specify a main or “<text:span text:style-name="T51">common</text:span>” font for use in the app (by default). Vous pouvez également choisir de spécifier un certain nombre d&apos;autres polices (en utilisant l&apos;onglet <text:span text:style-name="T51">Fichiers de police</text:span> qui seront intégrées dans l&apos;application pour être utilisées avec des livres différents ou des collections de livres. Si vous fournissez plusieurs polices, les utilisateurs pourront choisir entre elles dans la fenêtre contextuelle Apparence de texte et dans l&apos;éditeur de versets d&apos;images.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <table:table table:name="Table44" table:style-name="Table44">
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Table44.A"/>
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Table44.B"/>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table44.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table44.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P269" loext:marker-style-name="T63"><text:span text:style-name="T64">&lt;unk&gt;</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T65"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table44.B1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P269" loext:marker-style-name="T89"><text:span text:style-name="T89">To specify a default size for a font, set it at the book collection level under </text:span><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_The_Styles_tab" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T94">&lt;collection name&gt; </text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T75"></text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T94"> Styles </text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T75"></text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T94"> Default Text Size</text:span></text:span></text:a><text:span text:style-name="T89">.</text:span></text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="P269" loext:marker-style-name="T89"><text:span text:style-name="T89">To specify the range of text sizes available to the user, see </text:span><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_The_Text_Size" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T94">Appearance </text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T75"></text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T94"> Formatting </text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T75"></text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T94"> Text Size</text:span></text:span></text:a><text:span text:style-name="T89">.</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
   </table:table>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P72" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark text:name="_The_Font_Files"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871162"/>The <text:span text:style-name="T88">Font Files</text:span> tab<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871162"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Utilisez cet onglet pour spécifier tous les fichiers de police à partir desquels vous pouvez choisir pour la police principale et les polices disponibles sous l&apos;onglet <text:span text:style-name="T51">Fontes</text:span> au niveau du livre ou de la collection de livres. </text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Click <text:span text:style-name="T51">Add Font…</text:span> and specify a reference “<text:span text:style-name="T51">Family name</text:span>” for the font. Sélectionnez ensuite l&apos;une des polices communes proposées pour SAB ou l&apos;une de vos propres polices. Après avoir cliqué sur Terminer, la police sera ajoutée à la liste des polices disponibles à partir desquelles choisir.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Faites un clic droit sur un fichier de police dans la liste pour le supprimer ou modifier ses propriétés.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P72" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark text:name="_The_Font_Handling"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871163"/>The <text:span text:style-name="T88">Font Handling</text:span> tab<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871163"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Utilisez l&apos;onglet Gestion des polices pour activer le composant de gestion des polices de GeckoView.<text:bookmark-start text:name="_Hlk534358734"/> Si vous utilisez un script non-romain ou un script romain en combinant diacritiques, il est possible que les appareils Android n&apos;affichent pas correctement vos polices. Pour surmonter ces problèmes, essayez d&apos;utiliser la bibliothèque GeckoView.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P15" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">GeckoView est un composant de visionneuse de Mozilla qui remplace la visionneuse Android standard. Il peut rendre les polices Graphite correctement.</text:span><text:bookmark-end text:name="_Hlk534358734"/><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P15" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Dans les captures d&apos;écran ci-dessous, la visionneuse standard est utilisée dans l&apos;image de gauche et GeckoView est utilisé dans l&apos;image de droite. Notez les cercles pointillés sur la gauche, indiquant que la police n&apos;est pas correctement affichée.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P9" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P3" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:soft-page-break/><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr4" draw:name="Picture 2" text:anchor-type="as-char" svg:width="2.4244in" svg:height="4.3437in" draw:z-index="0"><draw:image xlink:href="SAB02/26.png" xlink:type="simple" xlink:show="embed" xlink:actuate="onLoad" draw:mime-type="image/png"/>
    </draw:frame><text:s/><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr4" draw:name="Image3" text:anchor-type="as-char" svg:width="2.4402in" svg:height="4.3437in" draw:z-index="0"><draw:image xlink:href="SAB02/27.png" xlink:type="simple" xlink:show="embed" xlink:actuate="onLoad" draw:mime-type="image/png"/>
    </draw:frame><text:s/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P15" loext:marker-style-name="T89"><text:span text:style-name="T89">Utilisation de la visionneuse standard utilisant GeckoView</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T89"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P9" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P9" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Les fichiers de la bibliothèque GeckoView nécessaires ajouteront au moins 55 Mo à la taille de votre application, donc n&apos;activez pas GeckoView à moins que vous ne sachiez que vous en avez besoin pour afficher correctement vos polices.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P9" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Vous constaterez que lorsque vous construisez un APK Android avec GeckoView, la taille de l&apos;APK sera d&apos;au moins 200 Mo de plus que celle de GeckoView. Ceci est dû au fait qu&apos;il contient les bibliothèques GeckoView pour quatre architectures de périphériques différentes (ARM 32 bits, ARM 64 bits, Intel 32 bits et Intel 64 bits). En pratique, les utilisateurs de votre application n&apos;ont pas besoin d&apos;installer un fichier aussi volumineux.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
   <text:list text:style-name="WWNum74">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P118" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">For </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T53">online app distribution</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">, you need to upload an AAB file (app bundle) to Google Play rather than an APK. Le fichier AAB contient toutes les bibliothèques GeckoView pour les quatre architectures de périphériques, mais quand un utilisateur installe une application depuis Google Play, Google créera un APK sur mesure pour eux, avec seulement les bibliothèques et les composants dont ils ont besoin. Le fichier AAB peut avoir plus de 300 Mo, mais la taille réelle de l&apos;application pour n&apos;importe quel utilisateur sera beaucoup plus petite.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P118" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">For </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T53">offline app distribution</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">, you can ask for Scripture App Builder to create multiple APKs, one for each device architecture. Do this on the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T53">App</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T76"></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T24">APK</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> tab.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> Chacun de ces APKs sera considérablement plus petit (environ 55 Mo supplémentaires pour GeckoView). Il vous suffit de choisir le(s) bon(s) à distribuer, selon les types de téléphones que les gens possèdent. Beaucoup de téléphones aujourd&apos;hui utiliseront l&apos;APK ARM 64 bits. Sinon, l&apos;APK ARM 32 bits est utilisé pour la plupart des téléphones plus anciens. Intel phones are less common, but it will depend on the phones being sold in your country.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P9" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P72" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark text:name="_The_Keyboards_tab"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871164"/>The <text:span text:style-name="T88">Keyboards</text:span> tab<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871164"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Utilisez l&apos;onglet <text:span text:style-name="T51">Claviers</text:span> pour spécifier un ou plusieurs claviers Keyman à inclure dans votre application. Cela permet aux utilisateurs d&apos;utiliser le clavier pour taper des notes, etc. dans leur langue. L&apos;onglet <text:span text:style-name="T51">Claviers</text:span> inclut des liens vers <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="https://keyman.com/developer" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link">Développeur Keyman</text:span></text:a> (pour créer vos propres claviers) et le site <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="https://keyman.com/" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link">Keyman</text:span></text:a>. Il vaut la peine de consulter le site pour voir si quelqu&apos;un a déjà créé le clavier que vous désirez.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Important :</text:span> Pour permettre à l&apos;utilisateur d&apos;utiliser un clavier, assurez-vous et sélectionnez-le au niveau de la Collection de Livres dans l&apos;onglet <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_The_Styles_tab" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Styles</text:span></text:span></text:a>.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P72" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871165"/>The <text:span text:style-name="T88">Lexical Models</text:span> tab<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871165"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Utilisez l&apos;onglet <text:span text:style-name="T51">Lexical Models</text:span> pour spécifier un ou plusieurs modèles lexicaux pour fournir du texte prédictif pour les claviers Keyman intégrés. L&apos;onglet <text:span text:style-name="T51">Lexical Models</text:span> inclut un lien vers le site <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="https://keyman.com/developer" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link">Développeur Keyman</text:span></text:a> pour la conception et la compilation de vos propres modèles.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P52" text:outline-level="2"><text:bookmark text:name="_Styles"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871166"/>Styles<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871166"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"><text:soft-page-break/>L&apos;un des puissants avantages de Scripture App Builder est la possibilité de créer une application entièrement contextualisée pour une langue et une culture cibles spécifiques. À cette fin, SAB donne au concepteur d&apos;applications beaucoup de contrôle sur les styles de texte et d&apos;interface. Pour voir des références et des explications spécifiques à tous les styles disponibles dans le SAB, voir <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_Appendix_3:_SAB" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Annexe 3</text:span></text:span></text:a>.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Chaque style a plusieurs champs qui peuvent être personnalisés, stockés comme des champs CSS sous-jacents. Les styles sont divisés en deux catégories principales : <text:span text:style-name="T51">Style de texte</text:span> et <text:span text:style-name="T51">Styles d&apos;interface utilisateur</text:span>. Vous pouvez également créer <text:span text:style-name="T51">Styles personnalisés</text:span>. Utilisez la fonction <text:span text:style-name="T51">Trouver</text:span> pour rechercher un style particulier à modifier. Si vous connaissez le marqueur USFM pour le style, vous pouvez essayer d&apos;utiliser cela pour la recherche. For example, if you want to modify the style of a line of poetry, search for either “<text:span text:style-name="T51">poetry</text:span>” or “<text:span text:style-name="T51">q</text:span>” which is the USFM poetry marker.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Chaque style liste les <text:span text:style-name="T51">Noms</text:span>, <text:span text:style-name="T51">Description</text:span> et <text:span text:style-name="T51">Libération</text:span>- les caractéristiques spécifiques du style. Double-cliquez sur un style pour afficher la boîte de dialogue <text:span text:style-name="T51">Modifier le style</text:span>. Utilisez l&apos;onglet <text:span text:style-name="T51">Propriétés de style</text:span> pour modifier le style et/ou l&apos;onglet <text:span text:style-name="T51">CSS</text:span> pour ajouter ou modifier des éléments de style spécifiques. Cliquez sur <text:span text:style-name="T51">OK</text:span> lorsque vous avez terminé. Le nom du style modifié sera maintenant affiché en <text:span text:style-name="T158">bleu </text:span>pour montrer qu&apos;il a été changé. Pour revenir aux valeurs par défaut, faites un clic droit sur le style et choisissez <text:span text:style-name="T51">Réinitialiser à</text:span>.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P24"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Le menu <text:span text:style-name="T51">Apparence </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T72">&lt;unk&gt;</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51"> Styles</text:span> permet de définir les styles « niveau de l&apos;application». Les styles peuvent être définis en 3 endroits : au niveau de l&apos;application, au niveau de la collection de livres et au niveau du livre. Par défaut, les styles définis au niveau de l&apos;application s&apos;appliquent à toutes les collections et tous les livres. Certains styles ne s&apos;appliquent qu&apos;à l&apos;application elle-même (par exemple, menus, panneau de navigation, etc.). Cependant, de nombreux styles, en particulier des styles de texte, peuvent être réglés individuellement pour des collections et/ou des livres spécifiques.</text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P73" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871167"/>The <text:span text:style-name="T88">Text Styles</text:span> tab<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871167"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Il s&apos;agit d&apos;une catégorie large qui contient de nombreux styles de marqueurs disponibles dans Paratext qui sont automatiquement transférés, et de nombreux autres éléments descriptifs et fonctionnels dans le contenu de l&apos;application. Celles-ci comprennent différentes catégories de texte comme les marqueurs de chapitre et de verset, la poésie, les tableaux, les en-têtes, les notes de bas de page, les liens, les mots de glossaire, etc. Également inclus dans les styles de texte sont les différents éléments pour les quiz (voir le document <text:span text:style-name="T93">Créer des applications avec des questionnaires</text:span>). Utilisez la fonction <text:span text:style-name="T51">Trouvez</text:span> pour rechercher un style particulier. Pour plus d&apos;informations, voir <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_Appendix_3:_SAB" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Annexe 3</text:span></text:span></text:a>.</text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P73" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871168"/>The <text:span text:style-name="T88">User Interface Styles</text:span> tab<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871168"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Les styles d’interface affectent généralement les éléments de l’interface utilisateur de votre application. Cela inclut les menus, les icônes, les boîtes de dialogue, les onglets et le tiroir de navigation. Pour plus d&apos;informations, voir <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_Appendix_3:_SAB" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Annexe 3</text:span></text:span></text:a>.</text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P73" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871169"/>The <text:span text:style-name="T88">Custom Styles</text:span> tab<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871169"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Utilisez le <text:span text:style-name="T51">Ajouter un style…</text:span> pour ajouter un style personnalisé.</text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P73" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871170"/>Définition des styles au niveau de la collection de livres ou du livre<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871170"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Pour modifier les styles d&apos;une collection de livres particuliers, cliquez sur <text:span text:style-name="T51">Books</text:span> <text:span text:style-name="T71">&lt;unk&gt;</text:span> <text:span text:style-name="T51">&lt;Collection Name&gt;</text:span> <text:span text:style-name="T71">&lt;unk&gt;</text:span> <text:span text:style-name="T51">Styles</text:span>. La zone de configuration affichera les onglets de style texte et interface avec les éléments qui sont applicables au niveau de la collection du livre. Vous pouvez également modifier un certain nombre d&apos;autres attributs pour la collection, y compris les suivants :</text:p>
   <text:list text:style-name="WWNum89">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P119">Text font</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P119">Default text size</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P119">Hauteur de ligne par défaut</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P119">Direction du texte (gauche-à-droite / droite-à-gauche)</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P119"><text:soft-page-break/>Code de la langue</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P119">Système numérique</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P119">Numéros de verset</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P119">Keyboard</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Pour modifier les styles d&apos;un livre en particulier, cliquez sur <text:span text:style-name="T51">Livres</text:span> <text:span text:style-name="T71">&lt;unk&gt;</text:span> <text:span text:style-name="T51">&lt;Collection Name&gt;</text:span> <text:span text:style-name="T51">&lt;Book name&gt; </text:span>puis choisissez l&apos;onglet <text:span text:style-name="T51">Styles </text:span>dans la zone de configuration à droite.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P52" text:outline-level="2"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871171"/>Formatage (chapitres, versets et taille du texte)<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871171"/></text:h>
   <text:h text:style-name="P72" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871172"/>The <text:span text:style-name="T88">Formatting</text:span> tab<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871172"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">L&apos;onglet <text:span text:style-name="T51">Formatage</text:span> permet de contrôler spécifiquement si les numéros de chapitre et de verset sont affichés et comment ils sont formatés. Il vous permet également de spécifier si les paroles de Jésus peuvent être affichées en rouge (si disponible dans le livre courant) et si elles sont en rouge par défaut. Si activé, ce paramètre est disponible pour être modifié par l&apos;utilisateur dans les paramètres de l&apos;application.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P72" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark text:name="_The_Text_Size"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871173"/>The <text:span text:style-name="T88">Text Size</text:span> tab<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871173"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">L&apos;onglet Taille du texte vous permet de modifier si l&apos;utilisateur peut ajuster la taille du texte dans l&apos;application et de fixer les limites pour modifier la taille du texte via « pincer pour zoomer ».</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P9" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:s/></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P52" text:outline-level="2"><text:bookmark text:name="_Changes"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871174"/>Changements<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871174"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Vous pouvez définir un ensemble d’expressions régulières « trouver et remplacer» des modifications à appliquer au texte dans vos fichiers source. Les modifications seront appliquées pendant le processus de compilation de l&apos;application et les fichiers source d&apos;origine ne seront pas modifiés. Par exemple, si vous avez ajouté des fichiers Paratext à partir d&apos;un dossier Paratext qui reçoit des mises à jour de votre équipe et que vous devez cependant modifier certains styles de texte ou marqueurs pour qu&apos;ils s&apos;affichent correctement dans l&apos;application, vous devriez appliquer ces modifications en utilisant la fonction Modifications. De cette façon, ils ne seront pas remplacés par les mises à jour Paratext, ou n&apos;affecteront pas le projet Paratext lui-même.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Les modifications appliquées à ce niveau affecteront l&apos;ensemble de l&apos;application. Vous pouvez utiliser l&apos;onglet Modifications <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_The_Changes_tab" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link">dans la collection de livres</text:span></text:a> ou réserver des menus pour les modifications à ces niveaux.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"><text:soft-page-break/>Une fois que les modifications ont été ajoutées, vous pouvez les désactiver ou les désactiver en cliquant dans la case à cocher <text:span text:style-name="T51">Activer</text:span>. Cliquez avec le bouton droit de la souris sur un élément pour le modifier ou le supprimer.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T51"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Ajouter un changement depuis la galerie…</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">SAB est fourni avec un ensemble limité de changements déjà définis. Cliquez sur le <text:span text:style-name="T51">Ajouter un changement à partir de la Galerie…</text:span> , sélectionnez celui que vous souhaitez utiliser et cliquez sur OK. </text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T51"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Ajouter une modification…</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Cliquez sur </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Ajouter une modification…</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> pour ajouter un élément de changement. Vous pouvez lui donner un nom descriptif et spécifier les expressions régulières à utiliser pour les champs de recherche et de remplacement.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P9" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P44" text:outline-level="1"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871175"/>The <text:span text:style-name="T88">Data &amp; Analytics</text:span> project menu<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871175"/></text:h>
   <text:h text:style-name="P52" text:outline-level="2"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871176"/>Analyses<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871176"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P10" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Si vous activez Analytics, l&apos;application se connectera à Internet de temps à autre pour envoyer des informations d&apos;utilisation de l&apos;application à un ou plusieurs comptes analytiques. Cela vous donnera une idée de la mesure dans laquelle les gens interagissent avec l&apos;application.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P9" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Les informations envoyées comprendront le modèle de l’appareil (comme ‘Google Nexus 7’, ‘Samsung Galaxy S4’), la version Android (comme ‘4. ), le fournisseur de réseau mobile et un emplacement approximatif (ville/pays). Aucune information personnelle n&apos;est incluse.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P9" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Vous pouvez configurer votre application pour envoyer des données d&apos;utilisation à l&apos;un ou plusieurs des moteurs d&apos;analyse suivants :</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P9" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <table:table table:name="Table45" table:style-name="Table45">
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Table45.A"/>
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Table45.B"/>
    <text:soft-page-break/>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table45.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table45.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_FCBH_Digest_Analytics" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T52">Analyse du résumé FCBH</text:span></text:span></text:a><text:span text:style-name="T52"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table45.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Envoie un condensé de données analytiques à la Foi arrive par l&apos;audition (FCBH).</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table45.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table45.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_S3_Digest_Analytics" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T52">S3 Digest Analytics</text:span></text:span></text:a><text:span text:style-name="T52"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table45.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Envoie un résumé de données d&apos;analyse à un seau Amazon S3 de votre choix.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table45.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table45.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_Amplitude_Analytics" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T52">Analytique d&apos;Amplitude</text:span></text:span></text:a><text:span text:style-name="T52"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table45.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Envoie des données à un compte d&apos;Amplitude de votre choix.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table45.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table45.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T52"><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_Firebase_Analytics_1" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T52">Analyse Firebase</text:span></text:span></text:a><text:span text:style-name="T52"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table45.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Envoie des données à un compte Google Firebase Analytics de votre choix.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
   </table:table>
   <text:p text:style-name="P9" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39"><text:line-break/>Pour configurer des analyses :</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
   <text:list text:style-name="WWNum34">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P378" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Sélectionner </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Activer l&apos;analyse</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P378" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Choose whether users can opt out of sharing user data</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P378" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Cliquez </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Ajouter un compte Analytiques…</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P378" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Choisissez un type de compte et entrez vos informations de compte analytique. </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
     <text:list>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:p text:style-name="P379" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Pour les Analyses FCBH, vous n&apos;avez pas besoin d&apos;informations d&apos;identification supplémentaires.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
      </text:list-item>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:p text:style-name="P379" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Pour S3 Digest Analytics, vous aurez besoin d&apos;un ID Bucket S3 et d&apos;un ID de pool d&apos;identité.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
      </text:list-item>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:p text:style-name="P379" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Pour les analyses d’amplitude, vous aurez besoin d’une clé API.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
      </text:list-item>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:p text:style-name="P379" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Pour Firebase Analytics, vous aurez besoin d&apos;un fichier de configuration google-services.json pour votre compte.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
      </text:list-item>
     </text:list>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:h text:style-name="P72" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark text:name="_FCBH_Digest_Analytics"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871177"/>Analyse du résumé de la FCBH<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871177"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T104">FCBH Digest Analytics est le service d&apos;analyse le plus simple qui ne nécessite presque aucune installation supplémentaire. </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">La foi vient en écoutant (FCBH) a mis en place un service d&apos;analyse à utiliser avec le constructeur d&apos;applications bibliques. En sélectionnant FCBH Digest Analytics comme type de compte, votre application </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T40">enverra un</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T90"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T40">petit résumé quotidien</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T53"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">(environ 300 octets pour chaque jour où l&apos;application est utilisée)</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T53"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T40">compressé données complètement anonymes</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> (pas de personnalité, téléphone, ou informations de localisation GPS) </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T40">via un transport chiffré</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> (https) </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T40">vers un centre de données Amazon en Asie. lorsque l&apos;appareil est connecté à Internet </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">(via cellule ou WIFI)</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T40"> pendant que l&apos;application est en cours d&apos;exécution.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P9" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Le FCBH utilise les données résultantes à deux fins : 1) Il apporte des contributions semestrielles aux organisations de détenteurs de textes, proportionnellement à l&apos;utilisation des enregistrements audio correspondants, et 2) ils montrent des données d&apos;utilisation aux visiteurs et aux donateurs pour encourager et inspirer la participation. L&apos;accès à ce service (données et tableaux de bord) est disponible pour les partenaires intéressés (par exemple les constructeurs d&apos;applications) afin qu&apos;ils puissent facilement suivre l&apos;utilisation. Envoyez un email à </text:span><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="mailto:sab-analytics@fcbhmail.org" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T39">sab-analytics@fcbhmail.org</text:span></text:span></text:a><text:span text:style-name="T39"> pour demander l&apos;accès.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P9" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:s/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Les données sont agrégées par un serveur FCBH et analysées à l&apos;aide de Splunk. Un instantané d&apos;un tableau de bord est ci-dessous. Le tableau de bord est interactif et permet de drill-down vers des applications ou des versions ou pays spécifiques. Le tableau de bord est un travail en cours et les partenaires du ministère intéressés sont les bienvenus pour contribuer ou construire leurs propres tableaux de bord sur le serveur Splunk.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P9" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr13" draw:name="Image1" text:anchor-type="as-char" svg:width="5.9846in" svg:height="3.6811in" draw:z-index="0"><draw:image xlink:href="SAB02/28.png" xlink:type="simple" xlink:show="embed" xlink:actuate="onLoad" draw:mime-type="image/png"/>
    </draw:frame><text:s/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P9" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:soft-page-break/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">While no location information is uploaded, Amazon’s servers record the IP addresses where data uploads occur from. FCBH then uses </text:span><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="https://www.maxmind.com/en/geoip2-databases" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Maxmind&apos;s</text:span></text:span></text:a><text:span text:style-name="T39"> free database to estimate device locations (at approximately 99% and 95% accuracy for country and city respectively).</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P9" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P72" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark text:name="_S3_Digest_Analytics"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871178"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="OLE_LINK24"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="OLE_LINK25"/>S3 Digest Analytics<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871178"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">S3 Digest Analytics uses the same mechanism as FCBH Digest Analytics to report a small digest of analytics data. However, you are responsible for hosting the Amazon S3 Bucket and processing the received data. Files are uploaded to the S3 Bucket and in a sub-folder based on the format (e.g. the current format is f1) and stored with a unique filename using a randomly generated </text:span><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Universally_unique_identifier" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T39">GUID</text:span></text:span></text:a><text:span text:style-name="T39"> as the basename. We are working with FCBH to package a Splunk configuration so that you can deploy your own server to analyze the data.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P9" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">To use S3 Digest Analytics, ensure you have admin permissions to an Amazon AWS account, and go to:</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P303" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="https://aws.amazon.com/console/" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T39">https://aws.amazon.com/console/</text:span></text:span></text:a><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P9" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">You will need to:</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
   <text:list text:style-name="WWNum36">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P380" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Sign In to the Console</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> at the top right of the screen.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P380" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Create an S3 Bucket.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
     <text:list>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:p text:style-name="P382" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Go to the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">S3</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> Service and click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Create bucket</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">, enter a Bucket name, select a Region near where the app will be distributed, and click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Next</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">.</text:span></text:p>
      </text:list-item>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:p text:style-name="P382" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">On the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Set properties</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> and </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Set permissions</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> steps, use the defaults and click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Next</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">.</text:span></text:p>
      </text:list-item>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:p text:style-name="P382" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Review the configuration and click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Create bucket</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">.</text:span></text:p>
      </text:list-item>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:p text:style-name="P382" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Copy the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Bucket name</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> into the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">S3 Bucket ID</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> field in Scripture App Builder.</text:span></text:p>
      </text:list-item>
     </text:list>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P381" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Create a Federated Identity.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
     <text:list>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:p text:style-name="P382" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Go to the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Cognito</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> Service and click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Manage Federated Identitites</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">. The first time you use this service it will start creating an identity pool for you. If the AWS account already has identity pools, then it will show a grid of existing one. If this is the case then click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Create new identity pool</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">.</text:span></text:p>
      </text:list-item>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:p text:style-name="P382" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Enter an </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Identity pool name</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">, click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Enable access to unauthenticated identities</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> (which allows users of the app to submit analytics without logging into some service), and click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Create</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">.</text:span></text:p>
      </text:list-item>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:p text:style-name="P382" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:soft-page-break/><text:span text:style-name="T39">Click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Show Details</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> to see the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Role Name</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> for the unauthenticated identities (in the next step, we will give them permission to put objects in the bucket created in the previous step). Click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Allow</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">.</text:span></text:p>
      </text:list-item>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:p text:style-name="P382" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Copy the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Identity pool ID</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> value inside the quotes in the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Get AWS Credentials</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> section of the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Sample code</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> page shown after completion of the previous step. Copy this string into the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Identity Pool ID</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> field in Scripture App Builder.</text:span></text:p>
      </text:list-item>
     </text:list>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P381" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Give permission to put data into the S3 Bucket.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
     <text:list>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:p text:style-name="P382" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Go to the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">IAM</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> Service and click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Roles</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> category.</text:span></text:p>
      </text:list-item>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:p text:style-name="P382" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Click on the Role created in step #3 (e.g. Cognito_&lt;IdentityPoolName&gt;Unauth_Role).</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
      </text:list-item>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:p text:style-name="P382" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Add inline policy</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">, click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Service</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> and choose </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">S3</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">.</text:span></text:p>
      </text:list-item>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:p text:style-name="P382" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Actions</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">, type in </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T89">PutObject</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> to search for actions, and check </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">PutObject</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> to select that action.</text:span></text:p>
      </text:list-item>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:p text:style-name="P382" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Resources</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">, use default Specific, click on </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Add ARN</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> link, enter the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Bucket name</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> from step #1 into the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Bucket name</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> field, click the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Any</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> checkbox at the end of the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Object name</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> field, and click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Add</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">.</text:span></text:p>
      </text:list-item>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:p text:style-name="P382" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Review policy</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">, enter a name in the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Name</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> field, and click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Create policy</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">.</text:span><text:bookmark-end text:name="OLE_LINK24"/><text:bookmark-end text:name="OLE_LINK25"/></text:p>
      </text:list-item>
     </text:list>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P9" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P72" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871179"/>Data Payload for FCBH and S3 Digest Analytics<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871179"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Both FCBH Digest Analytics and S3 Digest Analytics use the same JSON payload format. A complete sample data payload is below:</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P9" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P383" loext:marker-style-name="T173"><text:span text:style-name="T173">{&quot;startTime&quot;:&quot;20180306T0835Z&quot;,&quot;period&quot;:1440,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;12db7e3f-93d9-4370-b12b-fe048804e4f5&quot;,&quot;package&quot;:&quot;org.fcbh.hndwtc.n2&quot;,&quot;version_name&quot;:&quot;1.0.1&quot;,&quot;sessions&quot;:1,&quot;sessionMins&quot;:21,&quot;shares&quot;:3,&quot;dams&quot;:[{&quot;damid&quot;:&quot;HNDWTCN2DA&quot;,&quot;playMins&quot;:25,&quot;chaps&quot;:[&quot;MRK 1&quot;,&quot;MRK 1&quot;,&quot;MRK 2&quot;,&quot;MRK 2&quot;,&quot;MRK 3&quot;,&quot;MRK 4&quot;,&quot;MRK 4&quot;]}]}</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T173"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P384" loext:marker-style-name="T187"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P15" loext:marker-style-name="T191"><text:span text:style-name="T191">The payload is 296 bytes uncompressed and 224 bytes compressed. This sample is comprised of the following fields:</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T191"/></text:p>
   <text:list xml:id="list408221415" text:style-name="WWNum37">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P385" loext:marker-style-name="T191"><text:span text:style-name="T191">One day of activity (1440 minutes), starting on 2018-03-06.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T191"/></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P385" loext:marker-style-name="T191"><text:span text:style-name="T191">The id is a </text:span><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Universally_unique_identifier" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T191">GUID</text:span></text:span></text:a><text:span text:style-name="T191"> which was randomly generated on the phone when the app was first launched, enabling determination of how many unique installations of the app are in use (</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T192">but no user-identifying information</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T191">).  </text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P385" loext:marker-style-name="T191"><text:span text:style-name="T191">Package and version indicate which app is in use.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T191"/></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P385" loext:marker-style-name="T191"><text:soft-page-break/><text:span text:style-name="T191">This report was for a single 21-minute session. This (and other) values would be incremented if the app had been used multiple times within the reporting period.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T191"/></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P385" loext:marker-style-name="T191"><text:span text:style-name="T191">The user pressed Share in the app 3 times.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T191"/></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P385" loext:marker-style-name="T191"><text:span text:style-name="T191">The app played FCBH audio HNDWTCN2DA, which is a </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T57">Fileset ID</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T191"> from FCBH’s </text:span><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="https://biblebrain.com/" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link">Bible Brain</text:span></text:a><text:span text:style-name="T191">.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P385" loext:marker-style-name="T191"><text:span text:style-name="T191">The app played audio for 25 minutes. Since this is greater than 21 minute session time, the audio must have been playing while the screen was off for 4 minutes. Comparison of these fields enable some rough comparison of audio-only use, versus use of audio in combination with text.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T191"/></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P385" loext:marker-style-name="T191"><text:span text:style-name="T191">Mark 1-4 were played. Mark 1 and 4 being listed twice each indicates that the user pressed play twice in each chapter (and thus, also pressed stop in each).</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T191"/></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P9" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P72" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark text:name="_Amplitude_Analytics"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871180"/>Amplitude Analytics<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871180"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">To use Amplitude analytics, you will need to create an account. Go to:</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P386" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="https://amplitude.com/" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T39">https://amplitude.com</text:span></text:span></text:a><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P9" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">You will need to:</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
   <text:list text:style-name="WWNum35">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P388" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Sign Up</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> at the top right of the screen and create an account. You will receive an email to finish activating your account. Copy the link to your browser and go to the page and complete the activation process.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P388" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">You will be prompted to create a new organization. You can do that to invite team members to join your organization and access the data. You will also be prompted for some additional information.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P388" loext:marker-style-name="T52"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Create Project</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">, enter the project name and click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Create</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">. There will be a project for each individual app.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P388" loext:marker-style-name="T52"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Projects</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> on the left of the screen. This will show the list of projects and the properties including a long string of hexadecimal characters under the label </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">API Key</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">. </text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P388" loext:marker-style-name="T52"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Highlight and copy this string into the API Key field in Scripture App Builder.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52"/></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P307" loext:marker-style-name="T52"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P72" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark text:name="_Firebase_Analytics_1"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871181"/>Firebase Analytics<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871181"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P15" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">To configure Firebase Analytics, go to the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Data &amp; Analytics</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T71"></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Firebase</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> menu (see below).</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P9" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:soft-page-break/></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P65" text:outline-level="2" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:bookmark text:name="_Firebase_Analytics"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871182"/><text:span text:style-name="T39">Firebase</text:span><text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871182"/><text:span text:style-name="T39"> </text:span></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">The Firebase menu allows you to configure multiple options available with a Firebase account. You can specify which options to enable using the Firebase Features tab, copy in your Firebase configuration file (.json) in the Firebase Configuration tab, and set up Push Notifications and In-App Messaging under their respective tabs, if so desired.</text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P73" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark text:name="_Firebase_Features"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871183"/>The <text:span text:style-name="T88">Firebase Features</text:span> tab<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871183"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T51"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Firebase Analytics</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">To sign up for Firebase Analytics, ensure you have a Google account. </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P9" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P25" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">You will need to:</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
   <text:list text:style-name="WWNum52">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P391">Go to the Google Firebase website at <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="https://firebase.google.com/" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link">https://firebase.google.com/</text:span></text:a> and ensure you are signed in with your Google account.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P391">Click <text:span text:style-name="T55">Add project</text:span> to create a Firebase project for this app. </text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P391">In Step 1, you will need to give your new project a <text:span text:style-name="T55">Project name</text:span>.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P391">In Step 2, titled <text:span text:style-name="T55">Google Analytics for your Firebase project</text:span>, select <text:span text:style-name="T55">Set up Google Analytics for my project</text:span> and press <text:span text:style-name="T55">Continue</text:span>.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P391">In Step 3, titled <text:span text:style-name="T55">Configure Google Analytics</text:span>, click on the drop-down box and choose <text:span text:style-name="T55">Create a new account</text:span>. Give it a name, which can be the same as your Firebase project name. </text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P391">Check the boxes to confirm that you accept the analytics and data protection terms. Click <text:span text:style-name="T55">Create project</text:span> and wait a few seconds for the project to be created.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P391">Click the Settings button (a cog wheel icon near the top) and select <text:span text:style-name="T55">Project settings</text:span>.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P5"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr12" draw:name="Image18" text:anchor-type="as-char" svg:width="5.9236in" svg:height="1.2917in" draw:z-index="0"><draw:image xlink:href="SAB02/29.png" xlink:type="simple" xlink:show="embed" xlink:actuate="onLoad" draw:mime-type="image/png"/>
    </draw:frame><text:s/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P15"/>
   <text:list text:continue-numbering="true" text:style-name="WWNum52">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P391">On the <text:span text:style-name="T55">General</text:span> tab of the Settings, scroll down to the <text:span text:style-name="T55">My apps</text:span> section and click the Android app icon.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P391"><text:soft-page-break/>On the <text:span text:style-name="T55">Add Firebase to your Android app</text:span> page, enter your app package name and click <text:span text:style-name="T55">Register app</text:span>.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P391">Download the config file, <text:span text:style-name="T55">google-services.json</text:span>. That is all you need from the app registration. You can ignore the information on the rest of the screens and return to Settings. </text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P391">Go to the <text:span text:style-name="T55">Data &amp; Analytics</text:span> <text:span text:style-name="T76"></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T24">Firebase</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> page in </text:span>Scripture App Builder.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P391">Select <text:span text:style-name="T55">Firebase Analytics</text:span> as one of the features to use in the app.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P391">On the <text:span text:style-name="T55">Firebase Configuration </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T76"></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T24">Android</text:span> tab, click the <text:span text:style-name="T55">Browse</text:span> button and find the <text:span text:style-name="T55">google-services.json</text:span> config file that you have just downloaded from the Firebase console.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P305" loext:marker-style-name="T52"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P72" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871184"/>The <text:span text:style-name="T88">Firebase Configuration</text:span> tab<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871184"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Specify your Firebase Configuration file by clicking on </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Browse…</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> and selecting your downloaded </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">google-services.json</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> file.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P9" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P72" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871185"/>The <text:span text:style-name="T88">Push Notifications</text:span> tab<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871185"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P15">You can send direct messages over the internet to all the users who have your app installed on their phone.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P15">Such messages could include:</text:p>
   <text:list text:style-name="WWNum63">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P120">Sending greetings on special occasions.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P120">Sharing news of app updates, new resources and special offers.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P120">Encouraging people to use the app.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P15"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T51"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Setting up Firebase Cloud Messaging</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P9">To set up the push notifications feature:</text:p>
   <text:list text:style-name="WWNum64">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P121">If you have not already done so, follow the instructions on setting up a <text:span text:style-name="T55">Firebase project</text:span>, described in the section above on <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_Firebase_Features" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link">Firebase Features</text:span></text:a>.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:list text:style-name="WWNum65">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P122" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:soft-page-break/><text:span text:style-name="T39">In Scripture App Builder, go to the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T53">Data &amp; Analytics</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T76"></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T53">Firebase</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> tab and enable </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T53">Firebase Messaging</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P232" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:s/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T51"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Sending messages</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P15" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">To send a push notifcation message to all users of your app:</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
   <text:list text:style-name="WWNum66">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P123" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Go to the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T53">Firebase Console</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> for your Firebase project.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P123" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Select </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T53">Cloud Messaging</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> from the menu on the left of the screen.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P123" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T53">Send your first message</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P123" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Enter the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T53">Notification title</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> and </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T53">Notification text</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">, then click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T53">Next</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P123" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">In the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T53">Target</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> section, you want to send messages to users of your app. Click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T53">Next</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P123" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">For </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T53">Scheduling</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">, you want </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T53">Now</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> (unless you choose another time). Then click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T53">Next</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P123" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Accept all the other default options and then click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T53">Review</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> at the bottom of the screen.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P123" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Re-read your message to verify that all is OK, then click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T53">Publish</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> to send it. The message will be sent to all the app users (if they are connected or connect to the internet).</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P232" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P72" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871186"/>The <text:span text:style-name="T88">In-App Messaging</text:span> tab<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871186"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">To set up the In-App Messaging feature:</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
   <text:list text:style-name="WWNum96">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P124"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Enable </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Firebase In-App Messaging</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> under the </text:span><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_Firebase_Features" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Firebase Features</text:span></text:span></text:a><text:span text:style-name="T39"> tab</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P124">If you have not already done so, follow the instructions on setting up a <text:span text:style-name="T55">Firebase project</text:span>, described in the section above on <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_Firebase_Features" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link">Firebase Features</text:span></text:a>.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P124">Under the In-App Messaging tab, follow the instructions under <text:span text:style-name="T51">Configure In-App Messaging</text:span>.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P392" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P52" text:outline-level="2"><text:bookmark text:name="_User_Accounts_1"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871187"/><text:soft-page-break/>User Accounts<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871187"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P15" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">You can configure your app so that a user’s highlights, notes and bookmarks are saved to a database server. This means that the user can see them on another device, and they do not need to lose their work when they change their phone.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P16"><text:span text:style-name="T39">To enable this feature,</text:span> you need to do some configuration work in two places:</text:p>
   <text:list xml:id="list1305697073" text:style-name="WWNum50">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P394">within Scripture App Builder, and</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P393">in the Google Firebase console.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P232" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P73" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871188"/>Setting up User Accounts in Scripture App Builder<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871188"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P15" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">In Scripture App Builder:</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
   <text:list text:style-name="WWNum76">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P125" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Go to the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T53">Data &amp; Analytics</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T76"></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T53">User Accounts</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> tab.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P125" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Click on </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T53">Enable user accounts</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P232" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P73" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871189"/>Setting up the database in the Google Firebase console<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871189"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P15">To set up the database, which will contain the registered users’ information, you need to add Firebase to your app, create a database, set up authentication and configure rules.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P395" loext:marker-style-name="T56"><text:span text:style-name="T56">Add Firebase to your app</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T56"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P15">Follow the instructions in setting up a Firebase project, described in the section above on <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_Firebase_Features" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link">Firebase Features</text:span></text:a>.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P15"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P25" loext:marker-style-name="T56"><text:span text:style-name="T56">Create a Database</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T56"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">To create a database:</text:p>
   <text:list text:style-name="WWNum53">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P397">In your Firebase project console, select <text:span text:style-name="T55">Realtime Database</text:span> from the menu on the left of the screen (the option below Firestore Database).</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P397"><text:soft-page-break/>Click the <text:span text:style-name="T55">Create database</text:span> button.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P397">On the first page of <text:span text:style-name="T55">Set up database</text:span>, choose where you would like the data to be stored, then click <text:span text:style-name="T55">Next</text:span>.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P397">On the second page of <text:span text:style-name="T55">Set up database</text:span>, choose <text:span text:style-name="T55">Start in locked mode</text:span>, and click <text:span text:style-name="T55">Enable</text:span>.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"><text:s/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P390" loext:marker-style-name="T56"><text:span text:style-name="T56">Set up Authentication</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T56"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P26">To set up authentication:</text:p>
   <text:list text:style-name="WWNum58">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P398">In your Firebase project console, select <text:span text:style-name="T51">Authentication</text:span> from the menu on the left of the screen.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P398">Select the <text:span text:style-name="T51">Sign-in method</text:span> tab.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P398"><text:span text:style-name="T193">Click on </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51">Email/Password</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T193"> and enable this authentication method to allow users to sign up using their email address and password.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P398"><text:span text:style-name="T193">Click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51">Save</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T193"> to confirm your changes and return to the Sign-in method tab.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P26"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P399" loext:marker-style-name="T194"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P390" loext:marker-style-name="T56"><text:span text:style-name="T56">Configure Rules</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T56"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Rules are required to tell Firebase who will have access rights to read and write to the database. To configure the database rules: </text:p>
   <text:list text:style-name="WWNum59">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P400">In your Firebase project console, select <text:span text:style-name="T55">Realtime Database</text:span> from the menu on the left of the screen.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P400">Select the <text:span text:style-name="T51">Rules</text:span> tab.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P400">Change the rules to be as follows:</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P332" loext:marker-style-name="T178"><text:soft-page-break/><text:span text:style-name="T178">{</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T178"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P332" loext:marker-style-name="T178"><text:span text:style-name="T178">&quot;rules&quot;: {</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T178"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P332" loext:marker-style-name="T178"><text:span text:style-name="T178">&quot;authenticated-users&quot;: {</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T178"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P332" loext:marker-style-name="T178"><text:span text:style-name="T178">&quot;$uid&quot;: {</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T178"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P332" loext:marker-style-name="T178"><text:span text:style-name="T178"><text:s/>&quot;.read&quot;: &quot;$uid === auth.uid&quot;,</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T178"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P332" loext:marker-style-name="T178"><text:span text:style-name="T178">&quot;.write&quot;: &quot;$uid === auth.uid&quot;</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T178"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P332" loext:marker-style-name="T178"><text:span text:style-name="T178">}</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T178"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P332" loext:marker-style-name="T178"><text:span text:style-name="T178">}</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T178"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P332" loext:marker-style-name="T178"><text:span text:style-name="T178">}</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T178"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P332" loext:marker-style-name="T178"><text:span text:style-name="T178">}</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T178"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P22">This rule says that only authenticated users will have right to read and write their own data. Unauthenticated users will not be able to see or change anything, and authenticated users will not have the right to see or change someone else’s data. </text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:list text:continue-numbering="true" text:style-name="WWNum59">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P400" loext:marker-style-name="T193"><text:span text:style-name="T193">Click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51">Publish</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T193"> to </text:span>confirm<text:span text:style-name="T193"> your changes.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P73" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871190"/>The <text:span text:style-name="T88">Data Deletion</text:span> tab<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871190"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T167"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Google’s policies require apps with user accounts to provide a URL where users can request account deletion. See </text:span><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="https://support.google.com/googleplay/android-developer/answer/13327111/" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link">Understanding Google Play&apos;s app account deletion requirements</text:span></text:a> and fill in the <text:span text:style-name="T51">Data Deletion URL</text:span>.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P242" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P44" text:outline-level="1"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871191"/>The <text:span text:style-name="T88">Publishing</text:span> project menu<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871191"/> </text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"><text:soft-page-break/>The Publishing menu helps you prepare your app for publishing to the Play Store, as a Progressive Web App or as an e-book (EPUB).</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P52" text:outline-level="2"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871192"/>App Store<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871192"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Documentation coming soon. See the <text:span text:style-name="T51">App Publishing Checklist</text:span> and <text:span text:style-name="T51">Distributing Apps</text:span> PDFs under the SAB Help menu.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P54" text:outline-level="2"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871193"/>Web App (PWA)<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871193"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Documentation coming soon.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P54" text:outline-level="2"><text:bookmark text:name="_E-books_(EPUB)"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871194"/>E-books (EPUB)<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871194"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P10" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">As well as building a smartphone app, you can create e-books in EPUB format. EPUB documents are readable by a number of e-book readers on Windows, Mac, iOS and Android platforms.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P228" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P10" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">If you have timing files for your audio, the e-books can contain ‘Read Aloud’ text-audio synchronization. These are readable by a few EPUB 3 readers, such as </text:span><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="https://www.adobe.com/solutions/ebook/digital-editions.html" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Adobe Digital Editions</text:span></text:span></text:a><text:span text:style-name="T39"> or </text:span><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="https://www.edrlab.org/software/thorium-reader/" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Thorium Reader</text:span></text:span></text:a><text:span text:style-name="T39">.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P9" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">To create an EPUB e-book:</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
   <text:list text:style-name="WWNum8">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P401" loext:marker-style-name="T53"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Use the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T53">Table of Contents </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">tab to choose which items should be available in the table of contents</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T53">.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P402" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Use the Cover tab to choose a cover design. If you are creating separate e-books for each book, a different cover image can be specified for each book on the Cover tab of each individual Book page.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P402" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Go to </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T24">Publishing</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T76"></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T24">E-books (EPUB) </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16">and </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">click the button </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Create EPUB File..</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">. This will launch the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T53">Create EPUB Document</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> wizard. You can choose which book collection and which books to include. You can choose whether to create a single e-book containing all the books or whether you want to create a separate e-book for each book. The latter is the best option if you will have audio in the book, since otherwise a whole NT with audio would be a very large e-book.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P18" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">The generated EPUB documents will be saved in the default EPUB output folder. See </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Tools</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T76"></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Settings…</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T76"></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Default Folders</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:list text:continue-numbering="true" text:style-name="WWNum8">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P402" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Open the EPUB documents in your chosen e-book reader.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P9" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:soft-page-break/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P9" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T39">Scripture App Builder generates EPUB 3 documents which should be backwardly compatible to be able to be read using EPUB 2 readers. EPUB 3-only features such as the text-audio synchronization will only be seen on compatible readers.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P356" loext:marker-style-name="T151"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P3" loext:marker-style-name="T151"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr4" draw:name="Picture 166" text:anchor-type="as-char" svg:width="2.3866in" svg:height="4in" draw:z-index="0"><draw:image xlink:href="SAB02/30.png" xlink:type="simple" xlink:show="embed" xlink:actuate="onLoad" draw:mime-type="image/png"/>
    </draw:frame><text:s/><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr4" draw:name="Picture 165" text:anchor-type="as-char" svg:width="2.3866in" svg:height="4in" draw:z-index="0"><draw:image xlink:href="SAB02/31.png" xlink:type="simple" xlink:show="embed" xlink:actuate="onLoad" draw:mime-type="image/png"/>
    </draw:frame><text:s/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P4" loext:marker-style-name="T38"><text:span text:style-name="T38">Viewing an EPUB Read Aloud document in the Gitden Reader app</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T38"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P357" loext:marker-style-name="T151"><text:s/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P356" loext:marker-style-name="T151"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P3" loext:marker-style-name="T151"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr4" draw:name="Picture 164" text:anchor-type="as-char" svg:width="4.8957in" svg:height="3.4898in" draw:z-index="0"><draw:image xlink:href="SAB02/32.png" xlink:type="simple" xlink:show="embed" xlink:actuate="onLoad" draw:mime-type="image/png"/>
    </draw:frame><text:s/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P4" loext:marker-style-name="T38"><text:span text:style-name="T38">Viewing an EPUB Read Aloud document in the Readium Chrome extension</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T38"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P46" text:outline-level="1"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871195"/>The <text:span text:style-name="T88">Navigation</text:span> project menu<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871195"/></text:h>
   <text:h text:style-name="P66" text:outline-level="2"><text:bookmark text:name="_Contents_Menu"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871196"/>Contents Menu<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871196"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">When the user launches the app you might want to display a contents menu, giving them an easy way to jump to books and specific references. This can be an essential part of helping users engage with Scripture and locate other content in your app that otherwise might be hard to find e.g. front and back matter material, storybooks, a thematic index or glossary. For more information on setting the styles for the various contents menu elements, see </text:span><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_Contents_Menu_Styles" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T23">Appendix 3</text:span></text:span></text:a><text:span text:style-name="T16">.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P199" loext:marker-style-name="T16"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">The contents menu contains a list of images and titles and can have several levels as needed.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P204" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr10" draw:name="Picture 227" text:anchor-type="char" svg:x="1.8063in" svg:y="0.0728in" svg:width="1.8752in" svg:height="3.4736in" draw:z-index="20"><draw:image xlink:href="SAB02/33.png" xlink:type="simple" xlink:show="embed" xlink:actuate="onLoad" draw:mime-type="image/png"/>
    </draw:frame><text:s/></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P74" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark text:name="_The_Contents_Items"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871197"/>The <text:span text:style-name="T88">Contents Items and Screens</text:span> tab<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871197"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P20" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">Contents menus are comprised of Items (clickable elements), headings (non-clickable items) and screens (groups of items representing a level in a nested menu structure). Each menu has by default one screen representing the top level menu.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P205" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:soft-page-break/></text:p>
   <table:table table:name="Table46" table:style-name="Table46">
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Table46.A"/>
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Table46.B"/>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table46.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table46.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P269" loext:marker-style-name="T63"><text:span text:style-name="T64"></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T65"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table46.B1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P269" loext:marker-style-name="T89"><text:span text:style-name="T95">You can quickly add</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T89"> an existing book to the contents menu. Click on the book’s collection name in the project menu tree view. This displays the collection’s list of books in the Book Collection tab. Right-click on the book and select </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T95">Add to Contents Menu</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T89">. If you have more than one menu “screen” (see below), you can choose which screen to add it to.</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
   </table:table>
   <text:p text:style-name="P238" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P205" loext:marker-style-name="T16"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P20" loext:marker-style-name="T23"><text:span text:style-name="T23">Contents Menu Items</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23"/></text:p>
   <text:list xml:id="list2526317840" text:style-name="WWNum38">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P403" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">For each contents menu item you want to add, click the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Add Item…</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> button and follow the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Add Contents Menu Item</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> wizard to add the item to the screen.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:list xml:id="list205155579455504" text:continue-list="list408221415" text:style-name="WWNum37">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:list>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:list>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="P126" loext:marker-style-name="T23"><text:span text:style-name="T23">Single Clickable Items</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23"/></text:p>
        </text:list-item>
       </text:list>
      </text:list-item>
     </text:list>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P129" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">To add a single item (one item on its own row) choose </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Single Item</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> (the default) and click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Next</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16">. </text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P404" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">You can choose to target the following: a </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Book reference</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16">, </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Another menu screen</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> or </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Elsewhere.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P404" loext:marker-style-name="T23"><text:span text:style-name="T23">Book References</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P404" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr4" draw:name="Picture 1986647599" text:anchor-type="as-char" svg:width="4.8752in" svg:height="3.8811in" draw:z-index="0"><draw:image xlink:href="SAB02/34.png" xlink:type="simple" xlink:show="embed" xlink:actuate="onLoad"/>
    </draw:frame><text:s/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P404" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">For a book reference, you will need to specify the following:</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"/></text:p>
   <text:list text:style-name="WWNum39">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P407" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">The </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">target reference</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16">, such as Luke 15 verse 1.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P409" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">This reference can be a book name, or a book and chapter, or a book chapter and verse. If the book is not a Scripture book, you can still select which page to open. If you have multiple book collections, you can specify an associated layout.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P281" loext:marker-style-name="T103"/>
   <table:table table:name="Table47" table:style-name="Table47">
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Table47.A"/>
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Table47.B"/>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table47.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table47.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P269" loext:marker-style-name="T3"><text:span text:style-name="T66"></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T3"> </text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table47.B1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P269" loext:marker-style-name="T89"><text:span text:style-name="T89">If the book does not have a linked book in another collection (i.e. the 2 pane view would not be able to show the same book in another collection), then choose single-pane view.</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
   </table:table>
   <text:list text:continue-numbering="true" text:style-name="WWNum39">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P407" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">The </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">title</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> of the item, such as ‘The Lost Sheep’ (you can also specify alternate translations for the title and subtitle)</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P408" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">An optional </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">subtitle</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P408" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">An </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">image</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> (optional) – to appear to the left of the title.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P206" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr3" draw:name="Frame11" text:anchor-type="paragraph" svg:y="0.0583in" svg:width="4.75in" draw:z-index="27" loext:may-break-between-pages="true">
     <draw:text-box fo:min-height="0.0161in">
      <table:table table:name="Table48" table:style-name="Table48">
       <table:table-column table:style-name="Table48.A"/>
       <table:table-column table:style-name="Table48.B"/>
       <table:table-row table:style-name="Table48.1">
        <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table48.A1" office:value-type="string">
         <text:p text:style-name="P269" loext:marker-style-name="T42"><text:span text:style-name="T66"></text:span></text:p>
        </table:table-cell>
        <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table48.B1" office:value-type="string">
         <text:p text:style-name="P269" loext:marker-style-name="T89"><text:span text:style-name="T89">Try and make your contents menu item images the same dimensions. Alternatively, you can set the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T94">Image width</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T89"> percentages to all be the same on the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T94">Contents</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T89"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T94">Settings</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T89"> tab under </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T94">Contents Items Display</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T89">.</text:span></text:p>
        </table:table-cell>
       </table:table-row>
      </table:table>
     </draw:text-box>
    </draw:frame><text:soft-page-break/><text:s/></text:p>
   <table:table table:name="Table49" table:style-name="Table49">
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Table49.A"/>
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Table49.B"/>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table49.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table49.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P269" loext:marker-style-name="T195"><text:span text:style-name="T86"></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T87"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table49.B1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P269" loext:marker-style-name="T89"><text:span text:style-name="T89">You can now add an animated GIF as a contents menu image. This is useful to add things like sign language videos to the menu.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T89"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
   </table:table>
   <text:p text:style-name="P206" loext:marker-style-name="T16"/>
   <text:list text:continue-numbering="true" text:style-name="WWNum39">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P408" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">An optional </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Audio</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> clip to provide a brief description of the item (this will display a speaker icon that can be tapped to play the audio)</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P408" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">A layout (how the picture and text are arranged).</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"/></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P207" loext:marker-style-name="T16"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P405" loext:marker-style-name="T23"><text:span text:style-name="T23">Another Menu Screen</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P405" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">Choose an existing menu screen from the drop-down list box. You will need to first </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Add a Screen</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16">… from the main </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Contents Items and Screens</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> tab to choose this option.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P198" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:s/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P405" loext:marker-style-name="T23"><text:span text:style-name="T23">Elsewhere</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P405" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">Choose one of the locations in the drop-down list box:</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"/></text:p>
   <text:list text:style-name="WWNum113">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P131" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">the About Box</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"/></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P131" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">the Language and Layout screen</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"/></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P131" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">the Settings screen</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"/></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P131" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">the Reading Plans chooser</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"/></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P131" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">a PDF Document (specified under </text:span><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_Documents" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T16">Media &gt; Documents</text:span></text:span></text:a><text:span text:style-name="T16">)</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P131" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">a News Feed (specified under </text:span><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_News_Feeds" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T16">Engagement &gt; News Feeds</text:span></text:span></text:a><text:span text:style-name="T16">)</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P131" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">an Illustration (specified under </text:span><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_Illustrations" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T16">Media &gt; Illustrations</text:span></text:span></text:a><text:span text:style-name="T16">)</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P131" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">a website URL</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"/></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:soft-page-break/></text:p>
   <text:list text:continue-list="list205155579455504" text:style-name="WWNum37">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:list>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:list>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="P126" loext:marker-style-name="T23"><text:span text:style-name="T23">Headings</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23"/></text:p>
        </text:list-item>
       </text:list>
      </text:list-item>
     </text:list>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P406" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">You can add non-selectable headings or dividers in your lists of items in the menu. You may want to do this to group certain items under a header, or just to provide some decoration. To add a heading, choose </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Heading</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16">. Select a layout, choose an image, then add an optional title, subtitle and/or audio clip to play when its speaker icon is tapped. </text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P410" loext:marker-style-name="T23"><text:span text:style-name="T23"/></text:p>
   <table:table table:name="Table50" table:style-name="Table50">
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Table50.A"/>
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Table50.B"/>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table50.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table50.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P269" loext:marker-style-name="T3"><text:span text:style-name="T66"></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T3"> </text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table50.B1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P269" loext:marker-style-name="T89"><text:span text:style-name="T89">To make a decorative heading, create a landscape image and set its width percentage to be 100%. Do not add a title or subtitle.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T89"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
   </table:table>
   <text:list text:continue-numbering="true" text:style-name="WWNum37">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:list>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:list>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="P126" loext:marker-style-name="T23"><text:span text:style-name="T23">Several Items on the Same Row (Grids)</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23"/></text:p>
        </text:list-item>
       </text:list>
      </text:list-item>
     </text:list>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P129" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">To add multiple items on the same row, choose </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Grid</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> and click Next. You can then choose an optional heading (title and subtitle) above the row. Click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Next</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16">. Then, on the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Grid Menu Items</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> screen, add 2 or 3 items, one by one. Choose their target location, layout, image, title and subtitle.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P102" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr4" draw:name="Picture 1986647597" text:anchor-type="as-char" svg:width="2.3484in" svg:height="4.4846in" draw:z-index="0"><draw:image xlink:href="SAB02/35.jpg" xlink:type="simple" xlink:show="embed" xlink:actuate="onLoad"/>
    </draw:frame><text:s/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P129" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">To edit a grid, double-click on it in the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Contents Items and Screens tab </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16">view</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">. </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16">This will open the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Edit Contents Item</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> dialog box. Use the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Heading</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> tab to add/remove/modify a heading. Use the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Grid Menu Items</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> tab to rearrange the items by dragging them up or down. Double-click on a grid item to edit it.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P129" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">You can select 2 or 3 items in your contents menu, right-click and choose </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Group into Grid</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> to facilitate creating a grid of items. You can also select an already made grid, right-click and choose </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Ungroup to single items</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> to split the items back into separate elements.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:list text:continue-numbering="true" text:style-name="WWNum37">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:list>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:list>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="P127" loext:marker-style-name="T23"><text:span text:style-name="T23">A Carousel</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23"/></text:p>
        </text:list-item>
       </text:list>
      </text:list-item>
     </text:list>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P132" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">To add a rotating horizontal set of items, choose </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Carousel</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> and click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Next</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16">. You can then choose an optional heading (title and subtitle) above the row. Click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Next</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16">. Then, on the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Carousel Menu Items</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> screen, add items, one by one. Choose their target location, layout, image, title and subtitle.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P132" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">You can select several items in your contents menu, right-click and choose </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Group into Carousel</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> to facilitate creating a carousel of items. You can also select an already made carousel, right-click and choose </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Ungroup to single items</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> to split the items back into separate elements.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P133" loext:marker-style-name="T16"/>
   <text:list text:continue-numbering="true" text:style-name="WWNum37">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:list>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:list>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="P127" loext:marker-style-name="T23"><text:span text:style-name="T23">Verse of the Day</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23"/></text:p>
        </text:list-item>
       </text:list>
      </text:list-item>
     </text:list>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P132" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">To add the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Verse of the Day</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> to the menu, choose </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Verse of the Day</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> and then an optional heading and subtitle. After adding this item, double-click on it to add or change the background colour if desired.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P282" loext:marker-style-name="T103"/>
   <table:table table:name="Table51" table:style-name="Table51">
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Table51.A"/>
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Table51.B"/>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table51.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table51.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P269" loext:marker-style-name="T42"><text:span text:style-name="T66"></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T70"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table51.B1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P269" loext:marker-style-name="T89"><text:span text:style-name="T89">If you want to include it, you might consider having the Verse of the Day as the first item in the list of items in your menu as it is very prominent.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T89"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
   </table:table>
   <text:list xml:id="list205155906139097" text:continue-numbering="true" text:style-name="WWNum37">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:list>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:list>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="P127" loext:marker-style-name="T23"><text:span text:style-name="T23">News Feed</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23"/></text:p>
        </text:list-item>
       </text:list>
      </text:list-item>
     </text:list>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P132" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:soft-page-break/><text:span text:style-name="T16">To add one or more items from a </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">News Feed</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16">, select </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Feed</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16">, then choose an available </text:span><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_Notifications" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T16">News Feed</text:span></text:span></text:a><text:span text:style-name="T16"> and the number of items from the feed you would like to display.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:list text:continue-list="list2526317840" text:style-name="WWNum38">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P403" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">You can reorder the items on the screen by selecting rows in the table and dragging up or down.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"/></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P403" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">Double-click on an item to open the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T24">Edit Contents Item</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> dialog box. From here you can select one of the following tabs to edit one of the settings you have chosen: </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T24">Layout, Image, Titles, Background, Padding, Target, Audio, Languages</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16">.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P290" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">Note that </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T24">Padding</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> and </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T24">Languages</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> give you additional control over your menu item. </text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P202" loext:marker-style-name="T16"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P12" loext:marker-style-name="T24"><text:span text:style-name="T24">Padding</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T24"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P12" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">Use the Padding tab to adjust the space around the menu item.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P202" loext:marker-style-name="T16"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P12" loext:marker-style-name="T24"><text:span text:style-name="T24">Languages</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T24"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P12" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">If you have more than one interface language in your app, the Languages tab will appear. You can specify if a contents menu item only shows up in a particular language has been chosen. This is helpful if you want to provide several versions of a resource (e.g. a “how to use this app” book) in the different languages. To do this, specify in which of the available languages you want it to be shown (see example below):</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P290" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:s/><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr4" draw:name="Image4" text:anchor-type="as-char" svg:width="5.5in" svg:height="4.2453in" draw:z-index="0"><draw:image xlink:href="SAB02/36.png" xlink:type="simple" xlink:show="embed" xlink:actuate="onLoad" draw:mime-type="image/png"/>
    </draw:frame><text:s/></text:p>
   <text:list text:continue-numbering="true" text:style-name="WWNum38">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P403" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">Go to the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Contents Settings</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> tab to specify display formatting and navigation options for the menu.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P282" loext:marker-style-name="T103"/>
   <table:table table:name="Table52" table:style-name="Table52">
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Table52.A"/>
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Table52.B"/>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table52.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table52.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P269" loext:marker-style-name="T42"><text:span text:style-name="T66"></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T70"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table52.B1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P269" loext:marker-style-name="T89"><text:span text:style-name="T89">By default the contents menu will not show the item reference (e.g. chapter and verse). You can turn this on by selecting </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T94">Show target references</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T89"> in the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T94">Titles</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T89"> tab for each menu item.</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
   </table:table>
   <text:list text:continue-numbering="true" text:style-name="WWNum38">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P403" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">Select the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Viewer</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> tab to see how the contents menu will appear in the app.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P3" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr4" draw:name="Picture 3" text:anchor-type="as-char" svg:width="5.0764in" svg:height="3.4689in" draw:z-index="0"><draw:image xlink:href="SAB02/37.png" xlink:type="simple" xlink:show="embed" xlink:actuate="onLoad" draw:mime-type="image/png"/>
    </draw:frame><text:s/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P199" loext:marker-style-name="T16"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P199" loext:marker-style-name="T16"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T23"><text:soft-page-break/><text:span text:style-name="T23">Contents Menu Screens</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">In some cases, you might want to have multiple contents screens (nested groups of items), i.e. you select an item in the first screen and it takes you to a second contents screen.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P199" loext:marker-style-name="T16"/>
   <table:table table:name="Table53" table:style-name="Table53">
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Table53.A"/>
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Table53.B"/>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table53.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table53.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P269" loext:marker-style-name="T3"><text:span text:style-name="T66"></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T3"> </text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table53.B1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P269" loext:marker-style-name="T89"><text:span text:style-name="T89">Grouping your items under screens can really help users find and access the content in your app, especially if you have different types of books and/or extra-Biblical content like front and back matter, glossaries, Bible studies etc. It is recommended to sketch out a proposed layout for your menus and then create the screens and items necessary.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T89"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
   </table:table>
   <text:p text:style-name="P199" loext:marker-style-name="T16"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T39"><text:span text:style-name="T16">A screen is a group of items. Items on a screen can lead directly to books, or to other screens. </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">By default a contents menu has one implicit screen called “</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">HOME</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">.”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P233" loext:marker-style-name="T39"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">To add a contents screen:</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"/></text:p>
   <text:list text:style-name="WWNum40">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P411" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">Click the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Add Screen…</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> button and give the screen a name.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P411" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">You will need to link to this new screen from the screen a level above (its parent screen). Select the parent screen by clicking on it so it highlights. Click the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Add Item…</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> button for that parent screen, specify its target to be </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T23">Another menu screen</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"> and select the name of your new screen. This will mean that when the user taps on this item in the first screen they will be taken to your new screen.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P411" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">Add menu items to your new screen as described above.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"/></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P282" loext:marker-style-name="T103"><text:s/></text:p>
   <table:table table:name="Table54" table:style-name="Table54">
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Table54.A"/>
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Table54.B"/>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table54.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table54.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P269" loext:marker-style-name="T3"><text:span text:style-name="T66"></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T3"> </text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table54.B1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P269" loext:marker-style-name="T89"><text:span text:style-name="T89">Make sure that the screen to which you want to add an item is selected by clicking to highlight it on the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T94">Contents Items and Screens</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T89"> page. Then click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T94">Add Item…</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
   </table:table>
   <text:list text:continue-numbering="true" text:style-name="WWNum40">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P411" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><text:span text:style-name="T16">You can move items between screens by dragging item rows up or down.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"/></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P211" loext:marker-style-name="T19"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P74" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871198"/>The <text:span text:style-name="T88">Contents Settings</text:span> tab<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871198"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Use the Contents Settings tab to specify exactly how the contents menu works, including the title displayed (if any), what menu items are displayed and how users navigate between books and the contents menu.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T51"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Contents Menu Title</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"><text:soft-page-break/>Use this setting to choose what is displayed in the app toolbar while the contents menu is showing.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T51"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Contents Items Display</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Each item has a title, subtitle and a reference that shows which book chapter / page and verse the item is pointing to. You can choose which of these elements to display.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">You can also adjust the proportion of the menu item image and text.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P77" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871199"/>The <text:span text:style-name="T88">Contents Navigation</text:span> tab<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871199"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Use this setting to specify what type of navigation button is shown when a user is viewing a book and what happens when the user launches the app.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T51"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Navigation</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Use this setting to specify what sort of navigation button the app shows when the user is viewing the pages of a book.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T51"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Launch Action</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Use this setting to specify whether the app always launches to the contents menu, or to the last book viewed.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P78" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871200"/>The <text:span text:style-name="T88">More Settings</text:span> tab<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871200"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T51"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Image Resizing</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">You can specify the maximum pixel width of contents menu images to reduce their size, if necessary.</text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P74" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871201"/>The <text:span text:style-name="T88">Viewer</text:span> tab<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871201"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"><text:soft-page-break/>Use the viewer tab to get an indication of how each screen in the menu will appear.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P66" text:outline-level="2"><text:bookmark text:name="_Navigation_Drawer"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871202"/>Navigation Drawer<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871202"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">The navigation drawer is the menu that slides out from the left or right side of the screen, depending on the current <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_How_can_I_2" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link">text direction</text:span></text:a> setting. This menu can also be accessed via the “hamburger” menu (three horizontal lines) in the menu bar.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P75" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871203"/>The <text:span text:style-name="T88">Menu Items</text:span> tab<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871203"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">As an aid to the user, you can add items to the navigation drawer that point to various, useful elements that can aid in helping the user go further in their studies or get answers to their questions.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <table:table table:name="Table55" table:style-name="Table55">
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Table55.A"/>
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Table55.B"/>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table55.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table55.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P269" loext:marker-style-name="T3"><text:span text:style-name="T66"></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T67"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table55.B1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P269" loext:marker-style-name="T89"><text:span text:style-name="T89">As part of a broader, Scripture Engagement strategy, you can add links to language websites, Facebook pages, </text:span><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_Notifications" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T89">News Feeds</text:span></text:span></text:a><text:span text:style-name="T89"> and WhatsApp groups.</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
   </table:table>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">To add an item, click <text:span text:style-name="T51">Add Menu Item…</text:span> and choose from the list of possibilities. Be sure to add multiple translations of the menu item if you have multiple interface languages.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P75" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark text:name="_The_Settings_tab"/><text:bookmark text:name="_Settings"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871204"/>The <text:span text:style-name="T88">Settings</text:span> tab<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871204"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">The <text:span text:style-name="T51">Settings</text:span> tab allows you to specify which app settings the user can modify. The list of settings is determined by which options you have enabled in your app. For example, the <text:span text:style-name="T51">Verse of the Day</text:span> notification setting will only appear in the list if you have enabled Verse of the Day under the <text:span text:style-name="T51">Engagement</text:span> <text:span text:style-name="T71"></text:span> <text:span text:style-name="T51">Notifications</text:span> project menu. </text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Click Show next to each setting you want the user to be able to modify in the app. These will appear under the Settings menu item in the app’s navigation drawer.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">To modify the style of the settings menu, see <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_Styles" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Appearance </text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T72"></text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T51"> Styles</text:span></text:span></text:a>. The specific settings styles are listed in <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#_Settings_Styles" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Appendix 3</text:span></text:span></text:a>.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <table:table table:name="Table56" table:style-name="Table56">
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Table56.A"/>
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Table56.B"/>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table56.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table56.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P269" loext:marker-style-name="T3"><text:span text:style-name="T66"></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T67"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table56.B1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P269" loext:marker-style-name="T89"><text:span text:style-name="T89">To specify whether a setting option is turned on by default, see the respective setting’s menu item in the SAB project menu. E.g. see </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T94">Engagement </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T71"></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T94"> Notifications </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T71"></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T94"> Verse of the Day</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T89"> to turn it on by default.</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
   </table:table>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"><text:soft-page-break/></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P75" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark text:name="_Audio"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871205"/>The <text:span text:style-name="T88">Sharing</text:span> tab (sharing apps)<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871205"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T16">One advantage of a digital Bible over a printed one is that users can freely share the Scriptures with other people. SAB provides several, helpful ways to share an app with others.<text:span text:style-name="T16"> You can choose to allow the user to use any or all of them:</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T51"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Share link to app on Google Play</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">We strongly recommend publishing your apps to the Google Play store so that the diaspora can have access, even if your local context don’t have internet access. If you have published it, then use this setting to provide an easy way to share the link via email or social media (e.g. WhatsApp).</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T51"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Share link to app on website</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Enable this if you have your APK available to download from an external site <text:span text:style-name="T16">(e.g. a language-specific website for a translation project)</text:span>.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T51"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Share app installer file</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Enable this to share your app’s APK file directly<text:span text:style-name="T16"> with another device, e.g. by Bluetooth, Wifi transfer or email. This option is especially useful in contexts where not everyone has easy internet access and where you want to promote offline app sharing</text:span>.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P204" loext:marker-style-name="T16"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P3" loext:marker-style-name="T16"><draw:custom-shape text:anchor-type="char" draw:z-index="21" draw:name="AutoShape 138" draw:style-name="gr15" draw:text-style-name="P521" svg:width="0.5953in" svg:height="0.3024in" draw:transform="rotate (0.662876049907446) translate (0.364583333333333in 3.05833333333333in)">
     <text:p/>
     <draw:enhanced-geometry draw:mirror-horizontal="false" draw:mirror-vertical="false" svg:viewBox="0 0 0 0" draw:glue-points="?f5 0 0 ?f7 ?f5 ?f13 ?f14 ?f7" draw:text-areas="0 ?f8 ?f12 ?f9" draw:type="ooxml-rightArrow" draw:modifiers="50000 49253" draw:enhanced-path="M 0 ?f8 L ?f5 ?f8 ?f5 0 ?f14 ?f7 ?f5 ?f13 ?f5 ?f9 0 ?f9 Z N">
      <draw:equation draw:name="f0" draw:formula="min(logwidth,logheight)"/>
      <draw:equation draw:name="f1" draw:formula="100000*logwidth/?f0 "/>
      <draw:equation draw:name="f2" draw:formula="if(0-$0 ,0,if(100000-$0 ,$0 ,100000))"/>
      <draw:equation draw:name="f3" draw:formula="if(0-$1 ,0,if(?f1 -$1 ,$1 ,?f1 ))"/>
      <draw:equation draw:name="f4" draw:formula="?f0 *?f3 /100000"/>
      <draw:equation draw:name="f5" draw:formula="logwidth+0-?f4 "/>
      <draw:equation draw:name="f6" draw:formula="logheight*?f2 /200000"/>
      <draw:equation draw:name="f7" draw:formula="logheight/2"/>
      <draw:equation draw:name="f8" draw:formula="?f7 +0-?f6 "/>
      <draw:equation draw:name="f9" draw:formula="?f7 +?f6 -0"/>
      <draw:equation draw:name="f10" draw:formula="logheight/2"/>
      <draw:equation draw:name="f11" draw:formula="?f8 *?f4 /?f10 "/>
      <draw:equation draw:name="f12" draw:formula="?f5 +?f11 -0"/>
      <draw:equation draw:name="f13" draw:formula="logheight"/>
      <draw:equation draw:name="f14" draw:formula="logwidth"/>
      <draw:handle draw:handle-range-y-minimum="0" draw:handle-position="0 ?f8" draw:handle-range-y-maximum="100000"/>
      <draw:handle draw:handle-range-x-minimum="0" draw:handle-position="?f5 0" draw:handle-range-x-maximum="?f1"/>
     </draw:enhanced-geometry>
    </draw:custom-shape><text:s/><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr11" draw:name="Picture 174" text:anchor-type="as-char" svg:width="1.9953in" svg:height="3.5335in" draw:z-index="0"><draw:image xlink:href="SAB02/38.png" xlink:type="simple" xlink:show="embed" xlink:actuate="onLoad"/>
    </draw:frame><text:s/><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr4" draw:name="Picture 173" text:anchor-type="as-char" svg:width="2.0028in" svg:height="3.5465in" draw:z-index="0"><draw:image xlink:href="SAB02/39.png" xlink:type="simple" xlink:show="embed" xlink:actuate="onLoad" draw:mime-type="image/png"/>
    </draw:frame><text:s/><text:span text:style-name="T16"><text:line-break/> </text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"><text:s/></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P75" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871206"/>The <text:span text:style-name="T88">History</text:span> tab<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871206"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Enable the history screen so users can easily select previously viewed books and chapters. They can access the <text:span text:style-name="T51">History</text:span> list of saved locations under the app’s navigation drawer menu. For information on setting the styles for various elements of the history feature, see Appendix 3.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P75" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871207"/>The <text:span text:style-name="T88">Search</text:span> tab<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871207"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"><text:soft-page-break/>The Search function allows users to find words across all book collections. There are several options you can set to specify how searches take place.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T51"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Show Search icon and allow searching</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">If you enable this, the <text:span text:style-name="T51">Search</text:span> menu item will appear in the navigation drawer menu and the magnifying glass search icon will appear in the app menu, if there is room.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T51"><text:span text:style-name="T51">‘Match whole words’ is selected by default</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">You can choose whether or not users are restricted to searching for whole words.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T51"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Show ‘Match whole words’ option on the Search page</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">This allows the user to turn off or on the ‘match whole words’ functionality.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T51"><text:span text:style-name="T51">‘Match accents and tones’ is selected by default</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">You can choose whether or not users are restricted to searching using accents and tones, if there are any in the language.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T51"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Show ‘Match accents and tones’ option on the Search page</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">This allows the user to turn off or on the ‘match accents and tones’ functionality.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T51"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Show special character input buttons on Search page</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">If you are allowing searching matching accents and tones, it is very helpful to include a list of any special characters (that would require an accent or tone marker) to be available for the user to select from.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"><text:soft-page-break/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T51"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Specify the replacements and diacritics to remove…</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">If you are not requiring ‘Match accents and tones,’ it is important to specify which characters should have simple equivalents. You can either the syntax X &gt; Y, with X being the accented character and Y being the non-accented equivalent (e.g. à &gt; a) OR just specify the Unicode character number of the diacritic to remove.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P67" text:outline-level="2"><text:bookmark text:name="_Bottom_Navigation"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233871208"/>Bottom Navigation<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233871208"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">The bottom navigation bar provides a quick way for users to access various elements of the app. It can be used in addition to or instead of a contents menu, but there is a limit of five items.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">After selecting <text:span text:style-name="T51">Enable bottom navigation bar</text:span>, click <text:span text:style-name="T51">Add Button…</text:span> to add a button to the menu bar. For each button you can specify a name (with multiple translations if needed) and an icon. Once an element is added to the list in SAB, double-click on it to modify it.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr10" draw:name="Picture 1986647585" text:anchor-type="char" svg:x="1.9209in" svg:y="0.302in" svg:width="2.4165in" svg:height="4.5772in" draw:z-index="25"><draw:image xlink:href="SAB02/40.jpg" xlink:type="simple" xlink:show="embed" xlink:actuate="onLoad"/>
    </draw:frame><text:s/><draw:custom-shape text:anchor-type="char" draw:z-index="297" draw:name="AutoShape 160" draw:style-name="gr1" draw:text-style-name="P521" svg:width="0.5953in" svg:height="0.3024in" draw:transform="rotate (0.298974900866629) translate (1.25902777777778in 4.82916666666667in)">
     <text:p/>
     <draw:enhanced-geometry draw:mirror-horizontal="false" draw:mirror-vertical="false" svg:viewBox="0 0 0 0" draw:glue-points="?f5 0 0 ?f7 ?f5 ?f13 ?f14 ?f7" draw:text-areas="0 ?f8 ?f12 ?f9" draw:type="ooxml-rightArrow" draw:modifiers="50000 49253" draw:enhanced-path="M 0 ?f8 L ?f5 ?f8 ?f5 0 ?f14 ?f7 ?f5 ?f13 ?f5 ?f9 0 ?f9 Z N">
      <draw:equation draw:name="f0" draw:formula="min(logwidth,logheight)"/>
      <draw:equation draw:name="f1" draw:formula="100000*logwidth/?f0 "/>
      <draw:equation draw:name="f2" draw:formula="if(0-$0 ,0,if(100000-$0 ,$0 ,100000))"/>
      <draw:equation draw:name="f3" draw:formula="if(0-$1 ,0,if(?f1 -$1 ,$1 ,?f1 ))"/>
      <draw:equation draw:name="f4" draw:formula="?f0 *?f3 /100000"/>
      <draw:equation draw:name="f5" draw:formula="logwidth+0-?f4 "/>
      <draw:equation draw:name="f6" draw:formula="logheight*?f2 /200000"/>
      <draw:equation draw:name="f7" draw:formula="logheight/2"/>
      <draw:equation draw:name="f8" draw:formula="?f7 +0-?f6 "/>
      <draw:equation draw:name="f9" draw:formula="?f7 +?f6 -0"/>
      <draw:equation draw:name="f10" draw:formula="logheight/2"/>
      <draw:equation draw:name="f11" draw:formula="?f8 *?f4 /?f10 "/>
      <draw:equation draw:name="f12" draw:formula="?f5 +?f11 -0"/>
      <draw:equation draw:name="f13" draw:formula="logheight"/>
      <draw:equation draw:name="f14" draw:formula="logwidth"/>
      <draw:handle draw:handle-range-y-minimum="0" draw:handle-position="0 ?f8" draw:handle-range-y-maximum="100000"/>
      <draw:handle draw:handle-range-x-minimum="0" draw:handle-position="?f5 0" draw:handle-range-x-maximum="?f1"/>
     </draw:enhanced-geometry>
    </draw:custom-shape><text:s/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">There are six possible elements to link to:</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P17" loext:marker-style-name="T51"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Contents</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P17">This displays the contents menu screen, if there is one.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P17"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P17" loext:marker-style-name="T51"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Bible</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P17">This will display the last, current book being viewed, or can display any book in any collection. When adding the button you can specify the target book to open or modify it later under the button’s <text:span text:style-name="T51">Book</text:span> tab.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P17"/>
   <table:table table:name="Table57" table:style-name="Table57">
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Table57.A"/>
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Table57.B"/>
    <text:soft-page-break/>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table57.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table57.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P269" loext:marker-style-name="T3"><text:span text:style-name="T66"></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T67"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table57.B1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P269" loext:marker-style-name="T89"><text:span text:style-name="T89">If you have any non-Bible books in your app, it is best to rename the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T94">Bible</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T89"> menu item to be </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T94">Read </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T89">or</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T94"> Books</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T89"> or something similar.</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
   </table:table>
   <text:p text:style-name="P17"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P17" loext:marker-style-name="T51"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Plans</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P17">If reading plans are included in the app, this will display the reading plans selection screen.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P17"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P17" loext:marker-style-name="T51"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Search</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P17">If the Search function is enabled, this open the search screen.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P17"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P17" loext:marker-style-name="T51"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Settings</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P17">This will display the settings screen, allowing the user to modify the app settings.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P17"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P17" loext:marker-style-name="T51"><text:span text:style-name="T51">About</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P17">This will display the About box.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr2" draw:name="Frame12" text:anchor-type="paragraph" svg:x="-0.0035in" svg:y="0.0992in" svg:width="5.978in" draw:z-index="24" loext:may-break-between-pages="true">
     <draw:text-box fo:min-height="0.0161in">
